{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas","id":37226,"title":"Exigent Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-26T01:13:11-08:00","id":37226,"title":"Exigent Ideas","content":"I'm sure there are other threads with ideas for Exigents, but I didn't see one on page 1, so why not. I am not sure what is the exact number of Exigencies (?) a more powerful god can have, but since each Maiden has only 20, I think my (so far pretty much spitballing) interpretation is that no one outside of the Incarna has more than 15, Liminals/Gemitians/etc... notwithstanding. This is just for Exigents. Some ideas I recently came up with:<br /> <br /> Bride of Athlak: this is probably a given. It will depend on any changes to Athlak in 3E, but I can see the higher up Brides, those who don't retire from his service. He probably only grants it to a few people, but I'm guessing he has to pick carefully, since an Exigent might give too much of an advantage to one tribe over the other when it comes to fighting/cattle stealing.(if that's still a thing in 3E). Charms related to War, Melee and Presence I'm guessing, maybe with Ride for those God-blooded children of war aurochs that she's riding? :P Anima banner would of course be some kind of Minotaur-like thingy.<br /> <br /> Exigent of Exaltation, Chose of Lytek: this should be an interesting one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm guessing in his heyday Lytek had about 3 or 4 Exigents, maybe slightly more, to handle the sheer number of Exaltations and related baggage. With the Solar's gone, Lytek down-sized to one single Exigent, and even that one is on and off. I'll be curious what's Lytek's relations to the black market exaltations will be. Also whether he's responsible for Exigencies as well as Exaltations, but I'm going to go with 'yes' until someone from the dev team or one of the books says otherwise. With the re-emergence of the Solars, Lytek's work is becoming more and more and his purview is once again expanding. He might be looking to take on a second Exigent (or first, if he has currently none). Of course, he is still not all that powerful to provide adequate status and Essence for the Exigent, so he might need to take on some debts to make it happen. The Gold Faction would probably be offering candidates for him, even trying to spread his worship in some way to increase his station/power. The Bronze faction in the meanwhile would be looking at sneaking one of their own into his department, even as an Exigent perhaps, or curtailing Lytek's grab for support in some way covert way. An Exigent of Exaltation's (the Xs make it sound cooler!) Charms would be probably based on Bureaucracy (to better navigate the policies of Yu-Shan) and Lore (Lytek has access to the memories of each incarnation of that Exaltation, so I can see his Exigents being able to grant some memories to select Exalts of their past lives). Also possibly Occult, maybe Terrestrial or even Celestial level Sorcery? And since Lytek can manipulate the circumstances of a Exaltation minutely, I think if it's going to have Charms based on Abilities, than Occult might fit for this one as well. No idea for anima banner for this one though.<br /> <br /> Exigent of Gri-Fel, Wardens of the Imperial City: just like the idea of propping these guys down into a Terrestrial game set in the Imperial City. While Dragon-blooded and the Immaculate Faith might not particularly like Exigents (I think I saw a quote somewhere which said they are looked at as similar to God-blooded: unapproved mixing of gods and mortals, or something similar) they might grudgingly accept the Wardens: Immaculate Monks may beat Gri-Fel up, but c'mon he's the god of your city. Not a good idea to piss him off. They'd probably be a mix of beat cops and high society dilettantes or something. Charms based on Investigation, Socialize, Awareness and something? No detailed ideas, and nothing about their anima banners.<br /> <br /> What are your Exigent ideas so far? Also a question to anyone who knows the answer: do you know if Elementals can also have Exigents, not just gods,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T02:48:17-08:00","id":37253,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure elementals can't have Exigents. For one, them not having access to the Exigence encourages the social divide between gods and elementals, and since that tension's ripe for drama we shouldn't get rid of it. For two, them having access to the Exigence sorta steps on thematic toes belonging to the Dragonblooded without much reason that I can see. As always, though? Rule Zero applies.<br /> <br /> Just made up a Nobilis character who might work well as an Exigent. She's the Queen of the Mosquitoes. She's a cunning little swashbuckler who has the skill to sneak into pretty much anywhere...but doesn't really think it's any fun unless she gets caught, so she generally sabotages her own efforts at stealth. She's a trickster and a protective mother and she has supernaturally potent powers to annoy the hell out of her opponents. She suffers from an inability to keep a secret once she knows it, so she generally tries to whisper secrets into the ears of people in their sleep, so that she can indulge her compulsion to share the secret without actually giving it away. And, of course, being a Nobilis character, she can summon biblical plagues of mosquitoes that can devour cities, or drive nations mad with an eternal curse of annoying whining noises in their ears whenever they try to sleep, but if she were in Exalted I'd probably scale the power level down a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 12-26-2013, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T03:09:28-08:00","id":37259,"title":"","content":"On how many, I think it also depends on other factors beyond sheer power. An exigent that simply goes away after a single life is likely going to be less of an investment than one with solar style power-- Exigetnst hat can naturally breed, a'la Dragon blooded would probably be very close to solar power in difficulty-- after all, you're creating reproducing superweapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T03:24:22-08:00","id":37260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=37253#post37253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure elementals can't have Exigents. For one, them not having access to the Exigence encourages the social divide between gods and elementals, and since that tension's ripe for drama we shouldn't get rid of it. For two, them having access to the Exigence sorta steps on thematic toes belonging to the Dragonblooded without much reason that I can see. As always, though? Rule Zero applies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to respectfully disagree with you here. There are lots of other ways to underline the social divide between gods and elementals without shutting out a whole rake of character concepts that people might want to play. The entire point of the Exigents is for them the be the Exalted of Whatever You Want. That loses something if they become the Exalted of Whatever You Want (Except Those Guys). Just my two cents, of course.<br /> <br /> And now, to stop derailing the thread, I had an idea for the Exalted of Extirpation- a samurai known only as the surgeon who has cut out his fear and mercy and now wanders the world, cutting loose corruption with his daiklave of solid flame- no matter what the consequence/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/768-djehuty3","name":"djehuty3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T03:48:26-08:00","id":37263,"title":"","content":"Re: Exigents and Elementals: I'm leaning towards 'yes' mostly because of the Dragon-blooded and the Elemental Dragons as their patrons. Since they were allowed, I wouldn't be surprised if other elementals could be granted similar privileges. Of course, elementals have a higher difficulty in petitioning for the Exigency itself, and I think that underlines the social divide: even if the given Elemental has the power to have his/her Exigent, it might not get the shard/catalyst that's needed. He can ask for it, submit the proper forms in triplicate etc... but I can see that being rejected/lost. After all, it is just a lowly elemental, thinks the paper-shuffling god. It should know its place and not ask for such silliness. <br /> <br /> Which means elementals will turn towards the black market to get their shards, which can fuel some interesting stories imho.<br /> <br /> &quot;But officer, I have resubmitted my request five times through the last 300 years. I need an Exalted, I can't handle all of this. My papers are lost, and the Fair Folk were attacking. Now you're going to punish me for not giving up and dying? That's what passes as 'justice' nowadays?&quot;<br /> <br /> I haven't thought of self-perpetuating Exigencies and the toll they might take on the gods, that is a good point. Hm, I woner whether any of the non-Incarna were successful in creating something like that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T04:01:06-08:00","id":37266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas#post37226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure what is the exact number of Exigencies (?) a more powerful god can have, but since each Maiden has only 20, I think my (so far pretty much spitballing) interpretation is that no one outside of the Incarna has more than 15, Liminals/Gemitians/etc... notwithstanding.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=37263#post37263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Exigents and Elementals: I'm leaning towards 'yes' mostly because of the Dragon-blooded and the Elemental Dragons as their patrons. Since they were allowed, I wouldn't be surprised if other elementals could be granted similar privileges.</div> </div> </div> </div>The traditional Exalted Hosts are not Exigents, and neither are the Liminals and the Getimians; they're simply Exalted.<br /> <br /> &quot;Exigents&quot; refer, quite specifically, to the Chosen of the lesser gods, created through sacrifice and the blessing of the Sun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T07:34:56-08:00","id":37849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=37259#post37259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On how many, I think it also depends on other factors beyond sheer power. An exigent that simply goes away after a single life is likely going to be less of an investment than one with solar style power-- Exigetnst hat can naturally breed, a'la Dragon blooded would probably be very close to solar power in difficulty-- after all, you're creating reproducing superweapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But no Elemental Exigents (has that been even been confirmed?) makes sense on the basis that I have never known someone play a Dragon-Blooded because their character would be able to have superior babies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T08:20:19-08:00","id":37869,"title":"","content":"I think we've been told explicitly that only Gods can create Exigents. That said, there have likely been hundreds if not thousands of Exigents over the years, so the works of most of them have happened without dramatically altering the course of Creation's History, at least in some way that makes the setting lose cohesion without their presence.<br /> <br /> In other words, I'm pretty sure that Elemental Exigents won't be a thing come their hardcover. But there's nothing that would make it impossible or harm the setting to decide that this is a thing anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T08:32:39-08:00","id":37877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>horvagab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas#post37226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there are other threads with ideas for Exigents, but I didn't see one on page 1, so why not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/259-overshee","name":"Overshee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar259_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:29:18-08:00","id":37898,"title":"","content":"Overshee does have a point. There weren't any Exigent topics on the first page, but on the second page alone, we have:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/29335-who-can-grant-exigent-exaltations-who-can-be-granted-one?p=29574#post29574\">Holden talking about who can make Exigents.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/3070-fuel-for-exigents-the-homebrew-god-list\">A list of homebrewed gods.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/23608-exigents-for-you-and-me\">More discussion re: Exigents.</a><br /> <br /> And if we go all the way back to the third page (out of four), then there's some <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/15190-weird-exigent-ideas\">discussion of weird Exigents.</a><br /> <br /> Mind, it sounds like these are the sorts of guys who'll get a lot of discussion and a lot of topics going. But a.) I might as well link back to something relevant to what I said earlier, and b.) &quot;nothing on page one, let's just make a new thread!&quot; just feels a little lazy to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T11:55:46-08:00","id":37944,"title":"","content":"O_O <br /> <br /> Ouch, you're right guys. The only one I recalled was the 'weird Exigent' one off the top of my head, and I figured something less weird and more 'straight' would be needed for these. Sorry about the clutter then, and I'll avoid this in the future.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T18:35:19-08:00","id":39725,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking about an Exigent built around themes of <i>preservation, endurance</i> and <i>longevity</i>. I thought about this Exigent have access to Charms similar to Pattern-Restoring Touch and Chaos-Repelling Diagram as well as Charms to resist environmental hazards. Charms that could ward off decay and perhaps a Charm that could extend the lifespans of others (maybe mortals could live 150 years or so if touched by this magic). This would be a character with a 10 000 year lifespan tasked with preserving the past and the present to promote the cultural and material wealth of the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T22:29:03-08:00","id":41524,"title":"","content":"I wonder what the Exigent of a Forbidden God would be like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1634-sareteni","name":"sareteni","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T23:10:39-08:00","id":41541,"title":"","content":"Exigent of Nisela, Goddes of Justice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/278-elyon","name":"Elyon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar278_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T23:23:27-08:00","id":41545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sareteni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=41524#post41524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder what the Exigent of a Forbidden God would be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm blanking on what Forbidden Gods are. Just deities out of favor with Mister Sunshine and Yu-Shan as a whole, or something more specific?<br /> <br /> In any case, the Exigent produced is reflective of the god in question more than anything. Whatever traits Forbidden Gods tend to have in common may suggest certain traits in their Chosen, but I don't expect we'll see any explicit decrees. What sort of Forbidden God were you thinking about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T23:36:58-08:00","id":41550,"title":"","content":"I have several ideas for Exigents. I've got a few written up (sans charms and mechanics) since I don't know what 3rd edition will bring. <br /> <br /> Right now I am writing up the Chosen of Ashaya, the minor and otherwise unimportant goddess of the Hopeful Dreams of Children. The inspiration for these Exalted is drawn from comic books (like Spiderman or the X-Men), Sentai shows (such as Power Rangers and Kamen Rider) and magical girl shows (Sailor Moon, Precure, Madoka, etc). I have some pretty nifty ideas for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T00:42:01-08:00","id":41563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=41545#post41545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm blanking on what Forbidden Gods are. Just deities out of favor with Mister Sunshine and Yu-Shan as a whole, or something more specific?<br /> <br /> In any case, the Exigent produced is reflective of the god in question more than anything. Whatever traits Forbidden Gods tend to have in common may suggest certain traits in their Chosen, but I don't expect we'll see any explicit decrees. What sort of Forbidden God were you thinking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forbidden Gods were ones that were either loyal to the Primordials after the war, or simply too dangerous to Creation, so they got locked up. The only ones I can think of off the top of my head are the leech gods and the goddess of dreams-that-killed-you-in-your-sleep.<br /> <br /> Its one way to have antagonists that aren't Team Green, Black, or Rainbow.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1634-sareteni","name":"sareteni","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T01:08:16-08:00","id":41571,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GFppdq6vEPg\" target=\"_blank\">Chosen of Warstriders</a>.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IjnoM5-mnw\" target=\"_blank\">Chosen of Nanomachines</a>, Exigent of the Chayan gods with the impossible-to-spell name.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PyaVC8rHbp4\" target=\"_blank\">Chosen of Clothing</a> vs a Solar Exalt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T04:37:22-08:00","id":41643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=41550#post41550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have several ideas for Exigents. I've got a few written up (sans charms and mechanics) since I don't know what 3rd edition will bring.<br /> <br /> Right now I am writing up the Chosen of Ashaya, the minor and otherwise unimportant goddess of the Hopeful Dreams of Children. The inspiration for these Exalted is drawn from comic books (like Spiderman or the X-Men), Sentai shows (such as Power Rangers and Kamen Rider) and magical girl shows (Sailor Moon, Precure, Madoka, etc). I have some pretty nifty ideas for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Check out Steven Universe, if you haven't already. Might give you some ideas for this sort of Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:39:03-08:00","id":41705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AdamantineRapier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=41571#post41571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GFppdq6vEPg\" target=\"_blank\">Chosen of Warstriders</a>.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6IjnoM5-mnw\" target=\"_blank\">Chosen of Nanomachines</a>, Exigent of the Chayan gods with the impossible-to-spell name.<br /> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PyaVC8rHbp4\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chosen of Clothing</b></a> vs a Solar Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That show, I hate it but the fight sequences are so good","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxrkv14ojD_TQXU0RBvF33Q\" target=\"_blank\">Fool's Corner Productions</a>: Where we review Video Game, and eventually tabletop RPGs<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/461-kingcarnival","name":"KingCarnival","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar461_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-04T20:17:51-08:00","id":42664,"title":"","content":"I get the impression that you're usually only given one Exalt even if you're powerful, though there are surely exceptions and some Exigent Exaltations reincarnate like Celestial Exaltations.<br /> <br /> While I do have one Exigent idea based on a canon god (Zhuzhiao, if you're curious), I think that looking at major canon gods and then thinking about what kind of Exigents they might have is a fairly blunt and limited approach to what we've been given here. Part of what differentiates Exigents from God-Blooded is that they're defined less by their relationship to their patron, so while it <i>can</i> be interesting to look at major gods who could have cool exigents, I think it's generally more productive to think about what kind of exigents might be cool in themselves, and then reverse-engineer the god relationship. It's such a rich palette that it seems a shame to focus on the obvious NPCs.<br /> <br /> The way they handled Exigents was really smart, because it finessed them past two of the biggest pitfalls with the basic idea: the power level required to create Exigents, and the mystique associated with Exaltation. The Exigent spotlighted in the core book, who looks likely to be the lead sig, was created by a miscellaneous local harvest god. You can have an Exigent based on a <i>genius loci</i>, a rank-and-file disease spirit, a Storm Mother, whatever, and in the vast gulf between peons like that and titanic figures like Lytek and Nara-O you have middle-management gods with limited, esoteric domains like &quot;Eastern settlements reclaimed by nature&quot; and &quot;missives penned in the grip of passion&quot;. Moreover, the comments we've heard suggest that the line between the god and the Exalt can be somewhat loose -- Janest was empowered by a farm god, but she can cut through armies like wheat, because that's awesome. It's not so much that a harvest God should confer that power as that it's a cool power that can be slotted comfortably into her thematic. I think that we're likely to see that good exigents do not necessarily come from looking at a domain and then extrapolating powers in a direct, straightforward way.<br /> <br /> Beyond just looking at gods (named or otherwise), there are quire a few ways to brainstorm Exigents. You can start with a system gimmick you'd like to build a character type around and work backwards from there, look at parts of the setting that seem like a rich concept space, come up with something specifically for the plot or metaplot of the region you're playing in, think about a broad character style that might be fun to play, whatever. There's a ton of potential.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A postscript: it makes me cringe a bit every time I hear someone talk about an Exigent of Lytek, because it seems like one of those ideas that's bad and nearly impossible to do well, but has an inexorable appeal that will seduce dozens of people into trying it. I don't want to pick on horvagab specifically here, because I think all of us had the idea independently, and I'm sure that 10 years from now there will have been dozens of different takes on the concept. It seems like kind of a weird thing for Lytek to even do, and if you approach the situation from &quot;what makes the Chosen of Exaltation cool?&quot; or &quot;Why would I want to play the Chosen of Exaltation?&quot; there isn't a lot there relative to most concepts. The appeal seems to largely be that Lytek is a major NPC and there's a gee-whiz so-meta quality to it, and while that can be a valid starting point -- the quality of the finished product is mostly independent of what inspired you to start -- it's hard to imagine a more uphill battle to make something good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T08:28:43-08:00","id":44927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=42664#post42664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A postscript: it makes me cringe a bit every time I hear someone talk about an Exigent of Lytek, because it seems like one of those ideas that's bad and nearly impossible to do well, but has an inexorable appeal that will seduce dozens of people into trying it. I don't want to pick on horvagab specifically here, because I think all of us had the idea independently, and I'm sure that 10 years from now there will have been dozens of different takes on the concept. It seems like kind of a weird thing for Lytek to even do, and if you approach the situation from &quot;what makes the Chosen of Exaltation cool?&quot; or &quot;Why would I want to play the Chosen of Exaltation?&quot; there isn't a lot there relative to most concepts. The appeal seems to largely be that Lytek is a major NPC and there's a gee-whiz so-meta quality to it, and while that can be a valid starting point -- the quality of the finished product is mostly independent of what inspired you to start -- it's hard to imagine a more uphill battle to make something good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see how a less office-bound version of Lytek would be desirable, but the problem is that the roles I'm coming up with for this hypothetical character are observer and mentor figure which is terribly narrow for an Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T09:31:02-08:00","id":44942,"title":"","content":"You could always give them a fighting style based on studying their opponent to give them a little more conceptual space, it's still rather generic for a Chosen of Exaltation though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:26:06-08:00","id":45058,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the more I think about it, the more a Lytek Exigent as an NPC makes sense. The main reason such would be useful is because of Lytek's ability to filter and choose past memories, something his Exigent could also share. Though still far from PC material, though it could be an interesting addition to a Sidereal game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T12:43:52-08:00","id":45066,"title":"","content":"If I had to make an Exigent of Lytek \u2013 had to, because I wouldn't otherwise \u2013 I'd make them the Chosen of the Memory of Heroes. Theirs would be the power to invoke the dreams of the First Age, to awaken in themselves and reveal to others the glories of innumerable generations of heroes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-09T07:32:50-08:00","id":45579,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that the character concept with the one awesome power that defines their whole existence is more god blooded than Exalted rather than the difference between the two being mostly a matter of power levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T17:56:50-08:00","id":57793,"title":"","content":"My idea for the Exigent of Lytek is quite different.<br /> <br /> As the God of Exaltation itself and as the Right Hand of Power, he has only made one Exigent. His Exigent is the Prime Exigent. This Exalt does not have a specific set of Charms based upon the panoply of Lytek nor revolve around his relation to other Exalted, but rather each incarnation of the Prime Exigent develops a unique Charmset based upon the nature and spirit of the character. Lytek's Exaltation grants the power for its recipient to realize its own potential.<br /> <br /> In effect:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T10:42:56-08:00","id":64122,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how that's relevant to what Lytek actually does or how an Exaltation that helps you achieve your own potential is meaningfully different from a Solar Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:12:19-08:00","id":64142,"title":"","content":"The first Exigent I thought of is probably also up there on the list of things everyone considers (to the extent that it's been alluded to by Holden at least once): a Chosen of Han-Tha. That could get nasty fast.<br /> <br /> When I read back through the West book recently, it occurred to me that Tya is a pretty clear example of an Exigent, being Chosen by Storm Mothers (possibly as a group effort of several of them, so that none of them has to die). Of course, as soon as I thought that, then I wanted her not to be, so that a younger, more PC-able Tya could be Exigented instead.<br /> <br /> And, of course, speaking of major setting powers, the Great Forks Trio and the Syndics both have uses for powerful servants... and provide a neat contrast. If someone like Shield of a Different Day makes an Exigent, she wants everyone to know it, both due to vainglory and propaganda. But if the Syndics had Chosen, they'd keep them in the shadows, since those people would, by nature, have abilities which could reveal the identities of their patrons. Cool stuff.<br /> <br /> Rounding out the list of obvious concepts, if Exigents do reincarnate while keeping the same God's traits (which I find probable, but uncertain), I imagine that many, many people will be the deeply confused Chosen of Swan Dragon, trying to find the source of their powers, and figure out why this crazy old man keeps on showing up. Which, to be honest, is a pretty great subversion of the &quot;wise old mentor in disguise&quot; arc, since the old man really doesn't know much of anything, and the young hero has to nurture him back to wisdom. And, yes, I maintain this will be popular whether or not it winds up making any sense for Lesser Elemental Dragons to have Exigents. Who doesn't love Swan Dragon?<br /> <br /> But for myself, my favorite Exigent concept I've had so far is a former (mortal, obviously), Immaculate Monk, who was part of a group putting the boots to some uppity God. However, that God was really demanding worship so they would be strong enough to hold off the encroaching Fair Folk/undead/demon cult, and to that end, had managed to gets its hands on an Exigency. Facing defeat, it used the Exigency (dying in the process, like weaker gods do) not on someone it would have chosen, but on one of the the only people present - the monks beating down its spirit servants - and hoped for the best.<br /> <br /> The details there are obviously intentionally vague, for maximum use flexibility, though I do like to think the God is of a river, or a mountain, or or something - namely, something with fairly broad associations, but which does not suggest immediate combat mastery*. This, overall, seems like it hits a lot of good hooks to me, and moves me much more than the &quot;mortal Immaculate who, by sheer random chance, became a Solar&quot; thing which crops up everywhere. It has more of a connection between the Immaculate and Anathema sides of things, in my mind.<br /> <br /> * Typing this out, I think really it should be a God of Birds, or of Scholars, or similar. To justify superhaman observation/learning Charms which in turn allow for developing Enlightened Martial Arts based on the Mortal-version katas and having watched Exalted Monks for years, naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:30:13-08:00","id":64153,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of places to go with Swan Dragon, for darned sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Making a Cadre of Exigents, or even just one, to help him fight off the Fair Folk in the Contagion. That is a heck of a story right there. As an NPC, even better, that single Exigent searching out his/her Master after all these Centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:10:32-08:00","id":64191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=64142#post64142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first Exigent I thought of is probably also up there on the list of things everyone considers (to the extent that it's been alluded to by Holden at least once): a Chosen of Han-Tha. That could get nasty fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably wouldn't be a bad idea to swap out Solar Filial Wisdom for an Exigent Filial Wisdom.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T12:22:22-08:00","id":64203,"title":"","content":"Actually, I have feelings on that point.<br /> <br /> If Han-Tha is only a small part of your campaign, then by all means. The important thing about Filial Wisdom is that he serves as the heavy to make displacing a mere mid-power God a serious challenge to a Circle (well, okay, him and the fact that you're constantly being attacked by the assorted other nasty factions of Rathess).<br /> <br /> But if Han-Tha is a major, ongoing foe, giving him multiple different enforcers can only help, and I actually really like the duality of having one Solar who's insane and dangerous, but still very much of two minds on his master's agenda (and virtually everything else - see also, insane), and one handpicked champion who is someone Han-Tha got to select for their compatibility with this plan. Variety is the spice, and all that. Stir in shortsighted Dragon-Blooded mercenaries, messed-up Dragon Kings who have recovered a warped version of their ancient powers without the attendant wisdom, amenable Raksha nobles, etc. to taste.<br /> <br /> And, of course, if your plot is about Sidereals or someone rushing to stop Han-Tha from getting/using one or more Exigencies, it'd be a hilariously nasty surprise to let them arrive in time... only to learn that Han-Tha has a crazy dangerous Exalt already in place for security, and make them fight Filial Wisdom while still racing against time.<br /> <br /> The reason that Exigents are, by far, my favorite new Exalt type based on (the very little) information we currently have is the way they add more weight and options to themes the setting already had. Things that are already there don't necessarily ever have to change, go away, or be overshadowed, they just gain more interesting context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T15:25:10-08:00","id":64346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=64203#post64203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason that Exigents are, by far, my favorite new Exalt type based on (the very little) information we currently have is the way they add more weight and options to themes the setting already had. Things that are already there don't necessarily ever have to change, go away, or be overshadowed, they just gain more interesting context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No kidding. And unlike so many of the established splats - one of them shows up and you won't know -what- to expect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/448-dulahan","name":"Dulahan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T12:32:03-08:00","id":67335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=64122#post64122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how that's relevant to what Lytek actually does or how an Exaltation that helps you achieve your own potential is meaningfully different from a Solar Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just as much as any Exaltation is different from each other.<br /> Solars are the embodiment of perfection, Lunars with impossibility, Sidereals with Fate/Samsara/Esotericness.<br /> <br /> Lytek's dominion is that of Exaltation itself, which is to say the elevation of mortals to becoming Weapons of the Gods. What constraints and influence he has within that domain is a touchy subject that will never be resolved. As such, Exaltation, and thus Lytek's Exigent, represents the Embodiment of Potentiality. Each persons potential is unique to that individual and intrinsically so. Effectively Devil-Tigers without the Transhuman lens. While the difference between this and Solars is subtle, it is but one interpretation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/15.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2104-tenkage","name":"Tenkage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2104_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:15:33-07:00","id":488755,"title":"","content":"The Exigent of Leeayta, basically Dinosaur exalt. I need some paper to sketch this...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:27:53-07:00","id":488785,"title":"","content":"I know I mentioned Dutiful Nhan in a previous topic, the God of Forgotten Things and Dusty Corners who I wrote up for my game.<br /> <br /> His chosen would basically be a little Spawn and a little Batman and a little his own thing. His anima banner manifests differently than other chosen, forming a cloak and cowl that obscure his identity and billows ever-greater as he expends Essence. He tangles and trips up his foes (or slashes them; there is a definite touch of the feline to Nhan's visage and character, and so claws may apply), tucks pain and wounds away to forget them for now, and has the ability to dredge up the old memories you'd wholly forgotten about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T00:51:19-07:00","id":489140,"title":"","content":"one idea i had was to have an exigent that empowered two persons more or less giving them a kind of linked mind with the ability to transform into a weapon, meaning a whole lot of stunting capabilities <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, one moment there is one of them swinging around his daiklave suddenly in response to an attack his daiklave turns into a woman that now wields the grimcleaver that the first guy just turned into. aaaaah the stunting opportunities i love it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> though it would be a bit tricky to figure out what god gave them their power","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T07:02:47-07:00","id":489433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=488755#post488755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exigent of Leeayta, basically Dinosaur exalt. I need some paper to sketch this...</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't Arilak make a better patron of the dinosaur exigent. Either way I fully support this being a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/659-dominostro","name":"Dominostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar659_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-23T09:51:26-07:00","id":489615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dominostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=489433#post489433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't Arilak make a better patron of the dinosaur exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div> It could be too, why not?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T10:29:45-07:00","id":490693,"title":"","content":"IMO they offer different takes on the dinosaur idea.<br /> The creatures Arilak takes care of are implied to exist nowhere else, they shouldn't just be seen as megafauna in a world where they're a fact of life but as semi-mythical creature that shouldn't exist anymore.<br /> Leeayta in contrast as the Dragon King Goddess of territorial conquest reflects the end of that savage time where the Dragon Kings have discovered tools and aren't just fighting to survive anymore, they're flourishing and need the room to grow as a species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T11:18:17-07:00","id":490736,"title":"","content":"Really Leeyata would be the goddess of Dragon Kings. She doesn't have many ties to &quot;dinosaurs&quot; that I can think of beyond the idea that Dragon Kings are lizard people and dinosaurs were sort of like giant lizards.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile Arilak is the goddess of &quot;ancient terrible largely extinct reptile monsters of whom Tyrant Lizards and Claw Striders are the few survivorrs, other than those creatures she has hidden away.&quot; She's also the Goddess of the Southeastern Jungles, so she would have some powers related to the flora and fauna of the jungle, as well as dinosaurs, and possible even some Charms related to the savage tribesman that live there.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine and I have been shooting some ideas back and forth for a charmset for Arilak as that was the first god he thought of when he first heard about Exigents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:03:52-07:00","id":491612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=490736#post490736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> She doesn't have many ties to &quot;dinosaurs&quot; that I can think of beyond the idea that Dragon Kings are lizard people and dinosaurs were sort of like giant lizards.</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh? The Dragon King/Dinosaur connection seems really fucking obvious to me.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm sorry if that sounded rude, but that's honestly one of the most baffling things I've ever seen said on this forum because I'm pretty sure that if you showed them the Dragon King cover of Scroll of Fallen Races a child could figure it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-25-2015, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:43:00-07:00","id":491632,"title":"","content":"Raptok are dromaeosaurs. Anklok are bipedal ankylosaurs. Pterok are feathered pterosaurs and Mosok are mosasaurs, though. So technically only half are based on actual dinosaurs.<br /> But yeah, they're dinosaurs. I think the Player's Guide specifically uses &quot;dinosaur.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T14:48:53-07:00","id":491950,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about running a game shortly after 3E comes out with an Exigent of Siakal as a major villain early on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T15:05:24-07:00","id":492006,"title":"","content":"Siakal will have a canon Exigent, the Lady of Blood and Breakers, but probably not until the Exigent book comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T20:58:19-07:00","id":492273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=491612#post491612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eh? The Dragon King/Dinosaur connection seems really fucking obvious to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>When people think about dinosaurs, they're probably not thinking about a humanoid race of lizard people who live in Aztec-style empires and reincarnate through their souls to live their lives over and over.<br /> <br /> They're probably thinking of something more along the lines of this <img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/ksr/assets/003/142/121/5cdfb6a2653dcc284fedc3458e8a779f_large.jpg?1421283 359\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> YMMV of course, but if someone asked me, &quot;Does Exalted have dinosaurs and what do they look like?&quot; I would point them more towards Tyrant Lizards and River Dragons than towards Dragon Kings.I mean, yeah, Dragon Kings clearly were inspired by dinosaurs, but I feel that there are better examples that would line up to actual dinosaurs in the setting than Dragon Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:30:08-07:00","id":492307,"title":"","content":"Sure, they're dinosaur/pterosaur/mosasaur <b><i>people</i></b>.<br /> River dragons are more like mosasaurs.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T21:34:32-07:00","id":492310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=490736#post490736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really Leeyata would be the goddess of Dragon Kings. She doesn't have many ties to &quot;dinosaurs&quot; that I can think of beyond the idea that Dragon Kings are lizard people and dinosaurs were sort of like giant lizards. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Dinosaur is a pretty damend broad category which I think depending on the cladisitc definition is Triceratops, modern birds, their common ancestor and all of their descendents. Or Iguanadon and Megalasaur, their common ancestor and all of its descendents (same result). None of these definitions, however, include lizards at all. They're a kind of archosaur, which includes them, crocodilians and pterosaurs as more closely related than any are to Lepidasaurs, which were lizards, snakes, tuataras, turtles (maybe) and extinct large aquatic reptilian vertebrates like plesiosaurs and mososaurs were.<br /> <br /> If you mean dinosaur in the colloquial sense, then Dragon Kings still count since Mosok and Pterok are based on large Mesozoic dIapsids that went extinct with actual dinosaurs. But Ratpok and Anlkok are really dinossaurian, as noted already. Having feathers kind of puts one in that area too.<br /> <br /> Big reptilian critters, sure. But to note in the picture you refer to, only one of those is actually a dinosaur and it's not the thing that's actually a kind of lizard. And note also things like clawstriders do exist in the setting regardless.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T22:00:09-07:00","id":492332,"title":"","content":"Clawstriders, treestriders, tyrant lizards, 3-horned ox dragons, and beasts of resplendant liquids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T22:24:49-07:00","id":492341,"title":"","content":"Leeyata is going to give themes based around Dragon Kings (intelligent reincarnating Aztec lizard people) whereas Arilak will give themes based around ancient, titanic lizard-like creatures that are mostly extinct and include things like Tyrant Lizards. Dinosaurs (in our world) tend to resemble the latter more so than the former, so if you want to make an Exigent themed off dinosaurs, IMO Arilak would be a little more appropriate than Leeyata. <br /> <br /> If you make a Chosen of Leeyata, you'd probably have a few &quot;dinosaur&quot; themed powers (just like the Exigent of a Volcano god would probably have a few powers that are similar to the Exigent of a forge god - both involve heat to some degree), but most of your powers would be based around the savage and civilized Dragon Kings more so than the idea of ancient, nearly extinct lizard-beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T22:44:09-07:00","id":492363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=492006#post492006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Siakal will have a canon Exigent, the Lady of Blood and Breakers, but probably not until the Exigent book comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok... would it be possible for her to have 2 (without dying)? She is a pretty powerful spirit (Essence 7 IIRC?)...<br /> <br /> I had in mind a Blackbeard type pirate captain as her Exigent, sowing chaos and slaughter across the West.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5488-goldfaction","name":"goldfaction","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T00:11:15-07:00","id":492385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>goldfaction</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/37226-exigent-ideas?p=492363#post492363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, ok... would it be possible for her to have 2 (without dying)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering we're probably not getting hard mechanics for what kind of god can Exalt this many Exigents with these traits, I think it should be absolutely possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}